  "helpTitle": "Quick guide",
  "tourWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to TrailBuddy",
  "tourWelcomeText": "This is where the trails you have ridden live, and those of your buddies — nobody else’s. Three ways bring trails here: import a GPX, record a ride, connect with buddies.",
  "tourWelcomeStart": "Start the tour",
  "tourMapIntroTitle": "The map",
  "tourMapIntroText": "Your trails and your buddies’ trails live here, each line in the color of its difficulty. The tour shows what the map tells you — and what is behind the buttons.",
  "tourMapNavTitle": "The sections below",
  "tourMapNavText": "Trails: all of them as a list, search and filter. Buddies: who sees your trails — and you theirs. Profile: import, rides, areas and the quick guide.",
  "tourMapBadgeTitle": "The sign at the start",
  "tourMapBadgeText": "Every trail starts with its sign showing grade and character; the dot below points its arrow in the riding direction. A tap on the sign — or on the line — selects the trail, a second one opens its sheet.",
  "tourMapSheetTitle": "The trail sheet",
  "tourMapSheetText": "Length, elevation and the difficulty as your network sees it — a tap on the grade shows who rated it how.",
  "tourMapColorsTitle": "Color means difficulty",
  "tourMapColorsText": "Every line carries its trail’s difficulty like a ski run. The style of the line tells its condition: crumbly means worn, dashed means beaten up, faded means barely rideable. An orange edge means a report, a yellow one a new note. The legend on the left edge opens and closes at any time.",
  "tourMapLayersTitle": "What the map shows",
  "tourMapLayersText": "The top button: which trails the map shows, the official trails of the region, and places such as food stops, water and bike service.",
  "tourMapLayersSheetTitle": "Choose places and official trails",
  "tourMapLayersSheetText": "Official trails and way quality on or off, places by group. What is off here stays off until you turn it back on.",
  "tourMapOfflineTitle": "Maps without signal",
  "tourMapOfflineText": "The button below puts the map on your device — for out on the trail, where there is no signal.",
  "tourMapRailTitle": "The toolbar",
  "tourMapRailText": "Here you draw an area the app saves for the trail, or take one away; “My areas” manages them.",
  "tourMapPositionTitle": "To you and to us",
  "tourMapPositionText": "The position button brings the map to you — your location never leaves the device. Top right, the light bulb: report an idea or a bug; it becomes a public entry on GitHub.",
  "tourMapRecordTitle": "Record a ride",
  "tourMapRecordText": "The big button records a ride — door to door, only on your device, even without signal. Afterwards you split it into trails; only those go to your buddies.",
  "coachLater": "Later",
  "coachNotNow": "Not now",
  "coachNext": "Next",
  "coachShowMe": "Show me",
  "coachTargetLost": "What this step points at is not visible right now. “Next” moves on.",
  "coachPosition": "{position} of {count}",
  "coachSkip": "Skip",
  "coachDone": "Let's go",
  "tourSplitIntroTitle": "Split your first ride",
  "tourSplitIntroText": "The ride becomes trails: the app recognizes known ones and suggests new ones. Only the pieces you choose go to your buddies — never the whole ride.",
  "tourSplitKnownTitle": "Already known",
  "tourSplitKnownText": "Trails that you or your buddies already have are recognized by their line. They come pre-ticked and go out as a confirmation — that keeps the trail current.",
  "tourSplitTakeOverTitle": "Now yours",
  "tourSplitTakeOverText": "You are riding one of your buddies’ trails for the first time: name, grade and character are prefilled from your network. With your stars it becomes yours — without a rating the piece does not go out.",
  "tourSplitQuestionTitle": "Still true?",
  "tourSplitQuestionText": "Something was reported on this trail that nobody has confirmed yet. You were just there — one tap answers it, with the time of your ride.",
  "tourSplitCandidateTitle": "A candidate",
  "tourSplitCandidateText": "A piece that could be a new trail: a descent off the known ways, or marked on the go. Set start and end with the handles, the map follows along; name, grade and character go right here.",
  "tourSplitHomeTitle": "Close to home",
  "tourSplitHomeText": "If a piece starts or ends near the start or finish of your ride, the app tells you — a ride often starts at your front door, and a trail should not give it away. Move the handle away if needed.",
  "tourSplitNoRoadsTitle": "Save an area first",
  "tourSplitNoRoadsText": "The app only finds new pieces where it knows the ways — from a saved area. Save one over the ride (layers button on the map), then split it again from “My rides”.",
  "tourSplitPickTitle": "What the search misses",
  "tourSplitPickText": "A jump line, a flat flow trail? This puts a candidate over the whole ride; the handles do the rest.",
  "tourSplitSubmitTitle": "What goes to buddies",
  "tourSplitSubmitText": "Only the ticked pieces go out, as trails to your buddies. The ride itself stays on your device, under “My rides”.",
  "tourTrailsIntroTitle": "Your trails",
  "tourTrailsIntroChainTitle": "On to the trails?",
  "tourTrailsIntroText": "All trails of your network as a list: what you have ridden and what your buddies contribute. Here you find a trail faster than on the map.",
  "tourTrailsRowTitle": "Reading a row",
  "tourTrailsRowText": "Stripe and sign carry the difficulty; the word says whose trail it is — MINE or your buddies’ names. A tap opens the sheet.",
  "tourTrailsSheetTitle": "Numbers and profile",
  "tourTrailsSheetText": "Length, elevation, grade and the elevation profile below. A tap on the grade shows all ratings — and what S0 to S5 mean.",
  "tourTrailsGradeTitle": "Your rating",
  "tourTrailsGradeText": "Tap your own S grade and your stars here. What is shown is what your network says — not just you.",
  "tourTrailsContributionTitle": "What you contribute",
  "tourTrailsContributionText": "Name, character, rating, visibility, description and link — your contribution to the trail. “Only me” keeps it hidden from buddies.",
  "tourTrailsNoteTitle": "Tell what is going on",
  "tourTrailsNoteText": "A note says what is going on right now: a fallen tree, new jumps, with a photo if you like. Buddies see it with a yellow edge until they have read it. A closure or the condition is reported next to it.",
  "tourTrailsSearchTitle": "Search and narrow down",
  "tourTrailsSearchText": "Search by name and buddy, typos included; the chips narrow down by map view, S grade range, character or report. Next to them, the sort order. Except for the map view, the filter applies on the map too.",
  "tourTrailsImportTitle": "Bring in a GPX",
  "tourTrailsImportText": "The icon at the top right reads GPX or zip files from other apps. Short and downhill becomes a trail, a whole loop becomes a ride — which you then split into trails.",
  "tourBuddysIntroTitle": "Your buddies",
  "tourBuddysIntroChainTitle": "On to your buddies?",
  "tourBuddysIntroText": "Who sees your trails — and you theirs. Only direct buddies, nothing beyond; there is no public map.",
  "tourBuddysInviteTitle": "Invite someone",
  "tourBuddysInviteText": "Sends a link to TrailBuddy through your messenger app — with your username, so you are found right away.",
  "tourBuddysSearchTitle": "Looking for buddies",
  "tourBuddysSearchText": "Search by username or the exact email address. You see each other’s trails only once the request is accepted.",
  "tourBuddysRequestsTitle": "Open requests",
  "tourBuddysRequestsText": "Requests to you show up here with accept and decline; requests you sent can be withdrawn.",
  "tourBuddysRowTitle": "A buddy in the list",
  "tourBuddysRowText": "“n shared” counts trails you both know. The pencil gives the buddy a name only you see; the speech bubble opens your messages.",
  "tourBuddysConnectTitle": "When you connect",
  "tourBuddysConnectText": "When you connect, identical trails become ONE trail with two names, the rest is added. If you part ways, their trails disappear from your map again.",
  "tourExampleBadge": "Example",
  "tourExampleTrailName": "Example: Beech Slope",
  "tourExampleTrailStats": "1.8 km · ↓ 210 m",
  "tourExampleTrailLength": "1.8 km",
  "tourExampleTrailHint": "This is what a trail looks like once you have imported or recorded one.",
  "tourExampleBuddyName": "Example: Mira",
  "helpIntro": "The essentials in six steps. Everything else you will find by trying it out.",
  "helpImportTitle": "Importing trails",
  "helpImportText": "You bring in GPX or zip files from other apps through the icon at the top right of the “Trails” tab, or in your profile under “Import trails”. A short track that mostly goes downhill becomes a trail; a whole loop is a ride — you split it into trails with the scissors in the import. Only trails go to your buddies, never the whole ride.",
  "helpMapTitle": "Reading the map",
  "helpMapText": "The color of a line is its difficulty, like on a ski slope: green S0, blue S1, red S2, black from S3; a white dashed edge means S4 or S5, gray not rated yet, magenta uphill. The style of the line is its condition: solid means all good, crumbly worn, dashed beaten up, faded barely rideable. An orange edge means a report (closed, destroyed or changed), a yellow one a new note; dashed violet lines are official trails — the legend on the left edge of the map lays all of this out. Every trail starts with its sign, and below it a dot whose arrow shows the riding direction. A tap on the sign or on the line selects the trail — a small card appears at the bottom, a tap on it opens the sheet. A long press on the map offers “Route from here” and “Route to here”.",
  "helpRideTitle": "Recording and splitting a ride",
  "helpRideText": "In the Android app, the big button at the bottom right of the map records a ride — even without signal, and it stays on your device. On the way you mark with the flag where a trail starts and ends. Afterwards you split the ride: the app recognizes known trails, and you pick new pieces yourself. Exported as GPX, the ride loads into any other app. Before you go, you plan a loop with the loop button: tap trails (tap again to remove), parameters, list and area on the left, then compute — offline, from your saved areas; the loop then sits under “My rides”. “Navigate” shows it on the way: the map turns with you, the rest of the route and your distance to it are at the top, and “Back to the route” next to them leads you back; with the app in the background both are in the notification, and swiped home the map stays as a small window. In “My rides” a finished navigation continues at the top; every ride shows its bike — a tap switches it; swipe left to delete, a long press selects several. The web app has no recording.",
  "helpBuddysTitle": "Buddies and visibility",
  "helpBuddysText": "You see your trails and those of your direct buddies — nobody else’s; there is no public map. You find buddies in the “Buddies” tab by username or exact email. If two recordings are the same way, they become ONE trail, even with two names. What you set to “Only me” nobody else sees.",
  "helpContributionTitle": "Your contribution to a trail",
  "helpContributionText": "In the sheet of a trail you contributed yourself, you enter name, S grade, character, stars, visibility, description and a link under “My contribution”. “Report” says what applies right now — the {report} status (closed, destroyed, changed) and the condition; it is confirmed when you rode the trail or are on site. A note tells buddies what is going on and lights up yellow for them. The navigation icon at the top of the sheet hands the start of the trail to your navigation app; “To trail head” computes the way there itself — offline, from your saved areas, with elevation and time.",
  "helpOfflineTitle": "Without signal",
  "helpOfflineText": "The app shows your trails offline too, as of your last download. What you contribute or report without signal waits in the outbox and goes out as soon as you have signal again. For the map to show anything, save an area beforehand: the “Offline maps” button on the map, then draw; manage them under “My areas” in your profile — ideally at home on Wi-Fi.",
  "helpMapTour": "Show the tour on the map",
  "helpTabTour": "Tour: {tab}",
  "helpSplitTour": "Tour: splitting a ride",
  "helpSplitTourHint": "Record a ride first — the big button on the map. Then the tour uses it to show how a ride turns into trails.",
  "helpDiscover": "Discover features and tips",
  "safetyNoteTitle": "Safety note",
  "safetyNoteDialogTitle": "Before you start",
  "safetyNoteConfirm": "Got it",
  "safetyNote": "You ride at your own risk. TrailBuddy shows what you and your buddies have ridden — it does not tell you whether a way may be ridden or is safe right now. Respect closures, trail rules and nature protection on site. A buddy’s report is no clearance, and no report does not mean everything is open."
}
